     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in the US.\n- **Single dose:** 1700 mg is well above the usual maximum of about 850\u20131,000 mg per dose.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high raise the risk of severe GI effects and lactic acidosis.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This totals 2,550 mg/day and is the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1700 mg total per day.** That could be 850 mg twice daily with meals, or about 567 mg three times daily, which isn't a standard tablet size.\n- **Another dose.** Tell me the dose and frequency you want.\n\nIf you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and add a note with the rationale. I'd still suggest confirming it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
